    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">National identity</span> is the sense of belonging a person has to a nation, shaped by shared history, culture, language and symbols, and it strengthens the bond between citizens and their country.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of National Identity</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">National identity is the collective sense of belonging to a nation that citizens share, built on common experiences, values, symbols and aspirations.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Components of National Identity</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Examples in Nigeria</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>National symbols</td><td>The flag, the coat of arms, the national anthem and pledge</td></tr><tr><td>Shared history</td><td>The independence struggle, the civil war, and the journey to democracy</td></tr><tr><td>Language</td><td>English as the official language, alongside major and minor indigenous languages</td></tr><tr><td>Culture and tradition</td><td>Festivals, arts, cuisine, dress and customs shared or celebrated nationally</td></tr><tr><td>Common institutions</td><td>The constitution, the judiciary, the National Assembly and other national bodies</td></tr><tr><td>Shared values</td><td>Unity in diversity, as captured in the national motto</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of National Identity</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Promotes unity among people of different ethnic and religious backgrounds.</li><li>Builds patriotism and loyalty to the nation.</li><li>Provides a sense of belonging and purpose.</li><li>Helps resolve conflict by emphasising what citizens share in common.</li><li>Strengthens the country's image and standing internationally.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Challenges to National Identity in Nigeria</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Ethnic and religious divisions that compete with national loyalty.</li><li>Weak civic education on national symbols and history.</li><li>Regional and political favouritism that undermines a sense of fairness.</li><li>Insecurity and conflict that fracture social cohesion.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to list and explain at least four components of national identity, with Nigerian examples for each.</div>",
