    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">As a <span class=\"learn-keyword\">global citizen</span>, a Nigerian is expected to contribute not only to peace at home but also to peace and stability beyond the nation's borders, especially within Africa.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Global Peace</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Global peace refers to a state of harmony and the absence of violent conflict among and within nations worldwide, supported by cooperation, justice and mutual respect.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Nigeria's Role in Peacekeeping</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Mission / Platform</th><th>Nigeria's contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>United Nations (UN) peacekeeping</td><td>Nigeria has contributed troops to UN missions in countries such as the Democratic Republic of Congo, Darfur (Sudan) and Mali</td></tr><tr><td>ECOMOG (ECOWAS Monitoring Group)</td><td>Nigeria led peacekeeping interventions in Liberia and Sierra Leone during their civil wars in the 1990s</td></tr><tr><td>African Union (AU) peace operations</td><td>Nigeria contributes troops and funding to AU-led peace and security efforts across the continent</td></tr><tr><td>Multinational Joint Task Force (MNJTF)</td><td>Nigeria leads regional military cooperation with Chad, Niger, Cameroon and Benin against Boko Haram</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Why Nigeria Participates in Peacekeeping</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>To promote regional stability, since conflict in neighbouring countries can spill over into Nigeria.</li><li>To fulfil Nigeria's foreign policy commitment to Africa as the centrepiece.</li><li>To build international goodwill and diplomatic influence.</li><li>To uphold the principles of the UN and AU charters on collective security.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Citizens' Role in Promoting Global Peace</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Practising tolerance and respect for people of other nations, cultures and religions.</li><li>Rejecting hate speech, xenophobia and extremism.</li><li>Supporting humanitarian and peacebuilding initiatives.</li><li>Being informed and responsible participants in international discourse.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember specific examples — ECOMOG in Liberia/Sierra Leone and the MNJTF against Boko Haram — as concrete illustrations of Nigeria's peacekeeping role.</div>",
