    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Justice</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">fairness</span> are foundational values for any stable society, ensuring that every citizen is treated equitably under the law, regardless of status, wealth or background.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Justice and Fairness</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Justice means giving each person what is due to them, upholding what is right and lawful. Fairness means treating people impartially, without favouritism or discrimination.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Social Justice</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Social justice is the fair and just distribution of wealth, opportunities and privileges within a society, ensuring that all groups — regardless of ethnicity, gender, religion or class — have equal access to basic rights and opportunities.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Equity</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Equity differs slightly from equality: equality means treating everyone the same, while equity means giving people what they individually need to have fair access to opportunities, recognising that people start from different positions.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. The Rule of Law</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Principle of the rule of law</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Supremacy of the law</td><td>No one, including leaders, is above the law</td></tr><tr><td>Equality before the law</td><td>All citizens are subject to the same laws and legal processes</td></tr><tr><td>Due process</td><td>Legal procedures must be fairly and properly followed before punishment</td></tr><tr><td>Independent judiciary</td><td>Courts must be free from political or external interference</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Importance of Justice and Fairness</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Builds public trust in government and institutions.</li><li>Reduces conflict and social unrest.</li><li>Protects the vulnerable from exploitation and abuse.</li><li>Encourages investment and economic development.</li><li>Strengthens democracy and the legitimacy of leadership.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">6. Challenges to Justice and Fairness in Nigeria</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Corruption within the justice system.</li><li>Delays in court proceedings.</li><li>Unequal access to legal representation.</li><li>Political interference in judicial matters.</li><li>Discrimination based on ethnicity, gender or social class.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to distinguish 'equality' from 'equity' with a simple example — this distinction is a common exam focus.</div>",
