    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Ethics</span> refers to moral principles that guide right conduct, while <span class=\"learn-keyword\">integrity</span> is the quality of being honest and consistent in one's values and actions, even when no one is watching.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Ethics and Integrity</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Ethics is a system of moral principles concerning what is right and wrong in human conduct. Integrity is the practice of being truthful, consistent and principled, aligning one's actions with one's stated values.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Importance of Ethics and Integrity</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Builds trust between citizens, leaders and institutions.</li><li>Promotes accountability and transparency in public and private life.</li><li>Reduces corruption and abuse of office.</li><li>Strengthens personal reputation and credibility.</li><li>Supports fair and effective governance.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Challenges to Ethics and Integrity in Nigeria</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Widespread corruption and bribery in public institutions.</li><li>Weak enforcement of anti-corruption laws.</li><li>Cultural and social pressures that sometimes reward dishonest success.</li><li>Poor role modelling by some public officials.</li><li>Economic hardship that tempts individuals toward unethical shortcuts.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Role of Ethics in Governance</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Ethical principle</th><th>Role in governance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Transparency</td><td>Open and honest conduct of government business, allowing public scrutiny</td></tr><tr><td>Accountability</td><td>Leaders answer for their decisions and actions</td></tr><tr><td>Fairness</td><td>Equal and impartial treatment of all citizens</td></tr><tr><td>Honesty</td><td>Truthful reporting and communication from government to the people</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Promoting Ethics and Integrity</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Strengthening civic and moral education in schools.</li><li>Enforcing anti-corruption laws consistently and fairly.</li><li>Encouraging whistleblowing and protecting whistleblowers.</li><li>Rewarding ethical leadership and honest conduct publicly.</li><li>Modelling integrity within families and communities.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to explain how a lack of ethics and integrity specifically undermines good governance, using concrete examples such as bribery or embezzlement.</div>",
