    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">As citizens of an interconnected world, Nigerians must understand major global challenges — terrorism, migration and climate change — and how these issues affect citizenship responsibilities at home and abroad.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Terrorism</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Terrorism is the use of violence and intimidation, especially against civilians, in pursuit of political, religious or ideological aims. Nigeria has faced significant challenges from groups such as Boko Haram and ISWAP in the North-East, with effects including loss of life, displacement, and disruption of education and economic activity.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Migration</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Internal migration</td><td>Movement of people within a country, e.g. rural-to-urban migration</td></tr><tr><td>International migration</td><td>Movement of people across national borders, for work, study or asylum</td></tr><tr><td>Forced migration</td><td>Movement caused by conflict, disaster or persecution, producing refugees and internally displaced persons (IDPs)</td></tr><tr><td>Irregular/illegal migration</td><td>Movement without proper legal documentation, often associated with human trafficking and smuggling</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"learn-p\">Migration raises citizenship issues such as the rights of migrants, integration, remittances to home countries, and the loss of skilled workers (brain drain).</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Climate Change</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Climate change is the long-term alteration of temperature and weather patterns, largely driven by human activities such as burning fossil fuels. In Nigeria, effects include desertification in the North, flooding in coastal and riverine areas, and erosion in the South-East, all of which threaten livelihoods and food security.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Citizens' Responsibilities Regarding Global Issues</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Supporting peace-building and rejecting extremist ideologies.</li><li>Respecting the rights and dignity of migrants and displaced persons.</li><li>Adopting environmentally responsible practices (reducing waste, conserving energy).</li><li>Staying informed about global issues that affect local communities.</li><li>Supporting government and international efforts to address these challenges.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to link each global issue — terrorism, migration, climate change — to a specific Nigerian example and its effect on citizens.</div>",
