    "topic": "Nigeria's Role in International Affairs",
    "topicCode": "SS3-CIT-10",
    "module": "Citizenship in a Global Context",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Nigeria plays an active role in international affairs through its membership in major organisations such as the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">African Union (AU)</span>, the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">United Nations (UN)</span>, and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">ECOWAS</span>.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Nigeria and the African Union (AU)</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria was a founding member of the AU's predecessor, the OAU (1963), and remains a leading member of the AU.</li><li>Nigeria contributes significantly to AU peace and security initiatives.</li><li>Nigeria supports AU programmes such as NEPAD and the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA).</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Nigeria and the United Nations (UN)</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria joined the UN in 1960, shortly after independence.</li><li>Nigeria contributes troops to UN peacekeeping missions worldwide.</li><li>Nigeria participates in UN agencies and programmes addressing health, education, and development.</li><li>Nigeria has served as a non-permanent member of the UN Security Council on several occasions.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Nigeria and ECOWAS</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria was a key founder of ECOWAS in 1975 and hosts its headquarters in Abuja.</li><li>Nigeria has led regional peacekeeping through ECOMOG in Liberia and Sierra Leone.</li><li>Nigeria supports the ECOWAS protocol on free movement of persons, goods and services.</li><li>Nigeria plays a leading diplomatic role in resolving political crises among member states.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance of Nigeria's International Engagement</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Enhances Nigeria's influence and leadership role in Africa and globally.</li><li>Attracts international trade, investment and development assistance.</li><li>Supports regional peace and security, which benefits Nigeria directly.</li><li>Provides a platform to advocate for African interests on the world stage.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the founding dates: OAU 1963, UN membership for Nigeria 1960, ECOWAS 1975 — these are common factual exam questions.</div>",
