    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)</span> are 17 global goals adopted by the United Nations in 2015, to be achieved by 2030, addressing poverty, inequality, climate change and other challenges facing humanity.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Concept of the SDGs</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">The SDGs form a universal call to action to end poverty, protect the planet and ensure that all people enjoy peace and prosperity by 2030. They succeeded the Millennium Development Goals (MDGs), which ran from 2000 to 2015.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Selected SDGs</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Goal 1</td><td>No Poverty</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 2</td><td>Zero Hunger</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 3</td><td>Good Health and Well-being</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 4</td><td>Quality Education</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 5</td><td>Gender Equality</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 6</td><td>Clean Water and Sanitation</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 7</td><td>Affordable and Clean Energy</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 8</td><td>Decent Work and Economic Growth</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 13</td><td>Climate Action</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 16</td><td>Peace, Justice and Strong Institutions</td></tr><tr><td>Goal 17</td><td>Partnerships for the Goals</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Relevance of the SDGs to Nigeria</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria faces significant poverty and inequality challenges (Goals 1 and 10).</li><li>Food insecurity and malnutrition remain concerns in parts of the country (Goal 2).</li><li>Access to quality education and healthcare is uneven across regions (Goals 3 and 4).</li><li>Climate-related challenges — flooding, desertification — affect many Nigerian communities (Goal 13).</li><li>Weak institutions and corruption challenge progress on Goal 16.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Nigeria's Efforts Toward the SDGs</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Establishment of the Office of the Senior Special Assistant to the President on SDGs.</li><li>Alignment of national development plans with SDG targets.</li><li>Partnerships with international agencies and NGOs for implementation.</li><li>State-level domestication of SDG priorities into local development plans.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Role of Citizens in Achieving the SDGs</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Practising responsible consumption and environmental stewardship.</li><li>Supporting education and healthcare initiatives in their communities.</li><li>Holding leaders accountable for SDG-related commitments.</li><li>Participating in volunteer and community development efforts.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> You do not need to memorise all 17 goals, but know the total number (17), the target year (2030), and be able to discuss at least four goals in detail with Nigerian relevance.</div>",
