    "module": "Civic Participation",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Young people make up a large proportion of Nigeria's population, making the role of <span class=\"learn-keyword\">youth</span> in democracy, innovation and community life especially important for the nation's future.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Role of Youth in Democracy</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Participating in voter registration and elections once of age.</li><li>Engaging in civic education and political discourse.</li><li>Holding leaders accountable through advocacy and social media engagement.</li><li>Running for elective office or supporting credible candidates.</li><li>Participating in youth wings of political parties and civic organisations.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Youth and Innovation</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Nigerian youth have shown strong capacity for innovation, particularly in technology, business and the creative industries, contributing to sectors such as fintech, entertainment (Nollywood, Afrobeats) and agritech start-ups, which create jobs and drive economic growth.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Youth and Volunteering</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Platform / Activity</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>National Youth Service Corps (NYSC)</td><td>A mandatory one-year national service programme for graduates, promoting national integration and service</td></tr><tr><td>Community-based volunteering</td><td>Youth-led clean-up campaigns, literacy drives, health outreach</td></tr><tr><td>Youth advocacy groups</td><td>Organisations addressing issues such as good governance, education and climate change</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Challenges Facing Nigerian Youth</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>High unemployment and underemployment.</li><li>Limited access to capital and mentorship for entrepreneurship.</li><li>Political and social exclusion from major decision-making.</li><li>Inadequate investment in youth-focused education and skills training.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Supporting Youth Participation</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Lowering barriers to youth participation in politics (the #NotTooYoungToRun movement led to a 2018 constitutional amendment reducing age requirements for elective office).</li><li>Investing in skills acquisition and entrepreneurship programmes.</li><li>Creating platforms for youth voices in policy-making.</li><li>Encouraging mentorship between experienced leaders and young citizens.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the #NotTooYoungToRun movement and its outcome — the 2018 constitutional amendment lowering age requirements for certain elective offices.</div>",
