    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Despite progress, Nigerian citizens continue to face significant obstacles — corruption, insecurity and poor leadership — that undermine the full enjoyment of citizenship rights and the achievement of national development goals.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Corruption</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Corruption remains one of Nigeria's most persistent challenges, diverting public resources meant for infrastructure, education and healthcare into private hands, and weakening public trust in institutions.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Insecurity</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Form of insecurity</th><th>Example / region</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Terrorism and insurgency</td><td>Boko Haram and ISWAP activities in the North-East</td></tr><tr><td>Banditry and kidnapping</td><td>Armed attacks and abductions, especially in the North-West and North-Central</td></tr><tr><td>Farmer–herder conflicts</td><td>Clashes over land and resources across several regions</td></tr><tr><td>Secessionist agitation</td><td>Tensions in parts of the South-East and other regions</td></tr><tr><td>Urban crime</td><td>Robbery, cultism and gang violence in cities</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Poor Leadership</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Weak accountability mechanisms that allow poor performance to go unchecked.</li><li>Selection of leaders based on ethnicity, religion or patronage rather than competence.</li><li>Policy inconsistency as different administrations abandon predecessors' programmes.</li><li>Inadequate responsiveness to citizens' needs and feedback.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Effects of These Challenges on Citizens</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Loss of lives, displacement and psychological trauma from insecurity.</li><li>Reduced access to quality public services due to misused resources.</li><li>Erosion of trust between citizens and government.</li><li>Discouragement of investment, slowing job creation and economic growth.</li><li>Weakened sense of national unity and shared purpose.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Addressing the Challenges</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Strengthening anti-corruption institutions and enforcement.</li><li>Investing in security sector reform and community policing.</li><li>Promoting merit-based leadership selection and civic education.</li><li>Encouraging active citizen participation in governance and oversight.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to link each challenge to a specific effect on ordinary citizens, not just describe the challenge in the abstract.</div>",
