    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">This topic brings together the major themes studied across SS1 to SS3, helping students see Citizenship and Heritage Studies as one connected body of knowledge rather than a set of separate lessons.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Foundations of Citizenship (SS1–SS2)</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Meaning and acquisition of citizenship (birth, descent, registration, naturalisation).</li><li>Rights and duties of citizens.</li><li>Structures and institutions of government.</li><li>National symbols and values.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. National Identity and Heritage</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Components of national identity — symbols, shared history, language, culture.</li><li>Tangible, intangible and natural heritage, and its role in modern Nigerian life.</li><li>Balancing tradition with modern development.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Governance, Justice and Ethics</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Principles of good governance, the rule of law, and social justice.</li><li>The role of ethics and integrity in public and private life.</li><li>Institutions protecting human rights — NHRC, judiciary, NGOs.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Citizenship in a Global Context</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria's role in international organisations — UN, AU, ECOWAS.</li><li>Nigeria's contribution to peacekeeping and global peace.</li><li>Global issues affecting citizenship — terrorism, migration, climate change, the SDGs.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Civic Participation and Nation Building</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>The role of youth, civic entrepreneurship and civic competence.</li><li>Challenges facing Nigerian citizenship and strategies to address them.</li><li>National rebirth and transformation agendas.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Use this topic to identify which theme areas feel weakest to you, and revisit those specific topics for focused study before the examination.</div>",
