    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">As SS3 students prepare to leave secondary school, understanding how to take up active civic roles — through voting, volunteering and community service — becomes especially relevant.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Voting</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigerians become eligible to register and vote at age 18.</li><li>Voter registration is done through the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC), using the Permanent Voter's Card (PVC).</li><li>Informed voting requires understanding candidates' manifestos, past records and policy positions.</li><li>Voting is both a right and a civic responsibility that shapes the quality of leadership and governance.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Volunteering</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Area of volunteering</th><th>Example activity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Education</td><td>Tutoring younger students or teaching literacy in underserved communities</td></tr><tr><td>Health</td><td>Supporting community health outreach or awareness campaigns</td></tr><tr><td>Environment</td><td>Participating in clean-up exercises or tree-planting initiatives</td></tr><tr><td>Social welfare</td><td>Supporting orphanages, shelters or relief efforts for disaster victims</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Community Service</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Community service involves contributing time, skills or resources to address local needs without expecting direct payment. Beyond its immediate benefits, it builds leadership skills, empathy and a habit of civic engagement that lasts into adult life.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Other Ways to Prepare for Civic Roles</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Joining youth civic organisations or clubs while still in school.</li><li>Participating in debates, Model UN or student government, where available.</li><li>Staying informed about current affairs and public issues.</li><li>Developing skills in public speaking, teamwork and leadership.</li><li>Planning to undertake the National Youth Service Corps (NYSC) after tertiary education.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know the voting age (18) and the role of INEC and the PVC in Nigeria's electoral process — these are frequently tested facts.</div>",
