    "topic": "Global Citizenship and the Future of Nigeria",
    "topicCode": "SS3-CIT-20",
    "module": "Citizenship in a Global Context",
    "term": "Third Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">global citizen</span> is someone who recognises their membership in a broader world community, and acts with awareness of how local and global issues connect, while still being rooted in their national identity.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Global Citizenship</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Global citizenship is the idea that one's identity transcends national or regional boundaries, and that individuals have responsibilities toward humanity as a whole, in addition to their responsibilities as citizens of a particular nation.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Characteristics of a Global Citizen</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Awareness of global issues such as poverty, climate change and inequality.</li><li>Respect for diversity, human rights and cultural difference.</li><li>Willingness to participate in solving global problems, locally and internationally.</li><li>Responsible digital citizenship, given the connected nature of modern communication.</li><li>Commitment to sustainable practices that consider the wellbeing of future generations.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Active Participation in a Globalised World</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Example of active participation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Economy</td><td>Engaging in international trade, e-commerce or remote work</td></tr><tr><td>Technology</td><td>Using digital platforms responsibly to learn, connect and innovate</td></tr><tr><td>Culture</td><td>Sharing and celebrating Nigerian culture internationally while embracing global diversity</td></tr><tr><td>Environment</td><td>Supporting global climate action initiatives at the local level</td></tr><tr><td>Advocacy</td><td>Participating in global movements for human rights, peace or development</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. The Future of Nigeria in a Globalised World</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Nigeria's large youth population represents significant potential for innovation and leadership on the global stage.</li><li>Continued investment in education, technology and infrastructure will shape Nigeria's global competitiveness.</li><li>Strengthening governance and security will determine Nigeria's ability to attract global partnership and investment.</li><li>Nigerian citizens, as global citizens, can help shape a positive international image for the country through their conduct and achievements abroad.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to explain how global citizenship and national citizenship complement rather than contradict each other.</div>",
