    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">legacy</span> of Nigerian heritage refers to the lasting inheritance of culture, values and achievements passed from earlier generations, and the responsibility of the present generation to preserve and build upon it.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Continuity of Nigerian Heritage</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Many aspects of Nigerian heritage — languages, festivals, traditional institutions, arts and crafts — have continued across generations despite colonialism, modernisation and urbanisation, showing remarkable resilience.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Preservation of Heritage</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Method of preservation</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Museums and cultural centres</td><td>The National Museum, Lagos; the Nike Art Gallery</td></tr><tr><td>Documentation</td><td>Written and digital recording of oral histories, languages and traditions</td></tr><tr><td>Legal protection</td><td>National Commission for Museums and Monuments (NCMM) safeguarding heritage sites</td></tr><tr><td>Education</td><td>Teaching Nigerian history, languages and culture in schools</td></tr><tr><td>Festivals and cultural events</td><td>Ongoing celebration of traditional festivals that keep practices alive</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Modernisation of Heritage</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Fusion of traditional and contemporary styles in fashion, music (Afrobeats) and art.</li><li>Use of digital platforms to document and share indigenous languages and knowledge.</li><li>Adaptation of traditional dispute resolution and governance structures within modern frameworks.</li><li>Promotion of heritage tourism as an economic opportunity.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Challenges to Preserving the Legacy</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Loss of indigenous languages, some of which are endangered.</li><li>Inadequate funding and maintenance of heritage sites.</li><li>Erosion of traditional values under the pressure of rapid urbanisation.</li><li>Insufficient documentation of oral traditions before elder custodians pass away.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Responsibility of the Present Generation</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Young Nigerians today have a responsibility to learn, practise and transmit their heritage to the next generation, while also finding innovative ways — through technology, education and enterprise — to keep that heritage relevant and valued.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be able to name at least one Nigerian institution or method dedicated to heritage preservation, such as the NCMM or the National Museum.</div>",
