    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">As students prepare to leave secondary school, understanding the civic life, responsibilities and opportunities that await them as young adults is an essential final step in their citizenship education.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Civic Life After Secondary School</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Transitioning to tertiary education, vocational training, or the workforce, each with its own civic context.</li><li>Becoming eligible to vote and participate more fully in democratic processes.</li><li>Taking on greater personal responsibility for decisions, finances and conduct.</li><li>Engaging with wider society beyond the school environment — workplaces, communities, institutions.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Continuing Civic Responsibilities</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Responsibility</th><th>Example in adult/post-school life</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Obeying the law</td><td>Complying with regulations in the workplace, on the road, and in the community</td></tr><tr><td>Paying taxes</td><td>Once employed or running a business</td></tr><tr><td>Voting</td><td>Participating in elections at local, state and national levels</td></tr><tr><td>Community service</td><td>Volunteering time or skills to community causes</td></tr><tr><td>National service</td><td>Undertaking the NYSC after tertiary education, where applicable</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Opportunities for Growth and Contribution</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Further education and skills acquisition to improve employability.</li><li>Entrepreneurship and innovation opportunities, especially in technology and the creative sector.</li><li>Civic and political engagement, including eventually seeking leadership roles.</li><li>Mentorship — both receiving guidance from older citizens and later mentoring younger ones.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Carrying Citizenship Values Forward</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">The values, knowledge and skills developed through Citizenship and Heritage Studies — integrity, civic competence, respect for national identity and heritage, and global awareness — are intended to guide students throughout their adult lives, shaping them into responsible citizens who contribute meaningfully to Nigeria's development.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to connect this topic back to earlier ones — for example, explaining how civic competence (Second Term) applies directly to life after school.</div>",
